-- title:
--   Hecke eigenvalue systems in parabolic cohomology are cuspidal
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number and $S$ a set of natural numbers containing every prime divisor of $M$, and let $F$ be a field of characteristic zero. Let $c$ be an additive homomorphism from the group $\Gamma_0(M)$ — formally, the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M ⊤`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ cut out by the full subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, viewed additively — to $F$. Assume $c$ lies in [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62), i.e. $c(\gamma)=0$ for every $\gamma$ whose matrix has trace squared equal to $4$; assume $c \neq 0$; and assume that $c$ is an eigenvector for the cohomological Hecke operators [`CohCarrier.heckeT M ⊤ ℓ F`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L250) (defined by transfer along the conjugation map from the index-$\ell$ subgroup), in the sense that for each prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$ there is $a \in F$ with $T_\ell c = a \cdot c$. The conclusion is the existence of a ring homomorphism $\chi$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$ (a vacuous family here, by the hypothesis on $S$) — to $F$, such that $T_\ell c = \chi(T_\ell)\, c$ for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura statement in the form needed downstream: a system of Hecke eigenvalues occurring on a non-zero parabolic character of $\Gamma_0(M)$ with values in a field of characteristic zero is a system of eigenvalues of the weight-two cuspidal Hecke algebra away from $S$, so that every relation holding among the $T_\ell$ on $S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ holds among the eigenvalues. It is used in the auxiliary-level arguments comparing such eigenclasses with cusp forms, in particular in the vanishing statements for parabolic classes at auxiliary level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_exists_ringHom_heckeAlgebra_apply_smul_eq_heckeT_of_mem_parabolicHoms.lean

